rows.en:
Later, when we went up to the roof for science class, I thought I heard Aizawa's voice.
Several other students heard it too.
I wonder... did he die after all...?{p}

What about you?
Would you like to try...?{p}That's the end of my story.
Let's hear from the next person...{p}

But as he was about to head home, he found Kuwahata lying in wait for him at the school gate.
Aizawa did as Kuwahata told him and followed him up to the roof.
Kuwahata's revenge had begun.{p}

The next day, Aizawa lured a teacher up to the roof, saying that Kuwahata had pushed someone off.
"Where'd that Kuwahata go?"
Then the teacher leaned over the railing at the spot Aizawa pointed to and peered down.{p}

He decided not to push Kuwahata off.
Instead, he put his hands on the roof's railing and jumped down himself.
Leaving Kuwahata lying on the cold concrete of the roof...{p}

Aizawa's scream rang out.
And the answer had come.
Aizawa did not survive.{p}

This time too, he waited for an opening with the delinquent he had called out, then made him inhale chloroform he'd prepared in advance.
The delinquent went limp at once, without even a chance to resist.
Aizawa pushed him off, just as he had Kuwahata.{p}

He ran straight down the stairs to check.
The delinquent was dead.
"So Kuwahata must be dead too."{p}

The next day, the school was in an uproar.
The friend who had escaped from Aizawa had confessed everything.
All sorts of rumors spread around the school.{p}

But when they searched Aizawa's house, they found a diary recording everything that had happened in minute detail.
Astonishingly, it even described what happened in his final moments the day before, which he couldn't possibly have written.
As if he had foreseen that it would happen.{p}

"No... I'll pass."
{f:I|I} didn't have that kind of courage.
Who on earth was this Aizawa{f:?|?}
Hadn't he jumped{f:?|?}
And yet he was still turning up on the roof...
I felt that if I went up there now, something terrible would happen.
"Are you sure you don't want to go?"
Arai pressed me firmly.
{f:I|I} nodded silently and decided to hear the next person's story.{p}"Well then, let's move on..."{p}

...The next day, {f:I|I} told the club president what had happened and asked for the seven wonders feature to be cancelled.
The president had listened half in doubt at first, but on learning that the story of the vanished students was true, granted {f:my|my} request.
This was fine.
This was for the best{f:.|.}
Time passed, and {f:I|I} became a second-year.{p}

Another sharp pain shot through the back of my head.
.........
Thinking of being pushed off the roof, {f:I|I} felt my consciousness slowly, quietly fade away...{p}
